# Write Financial Guide Article

When the user asks to write a guide or article, follow this workflow.

## Purpose

Guide articles target long-tail keywords that link back to calculator pages. They provide deeper educational content for specific financial scenarios and improve the site's topical authority.

## Input

The user provides a topic (e.g. "how to save for a house down payment", "should I pay off mortgage early or invest").

## Step 1: Create Guide Directory

Create `src/app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx`:

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import Image from "next/image";
import Link from "next/link";
import { site } from "@/lib/site";

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "[Guide Title]",
  description: "[150 char description targeting the main long-tail keyword]",
  openGraph: {
    title: "[Guide Title] | " + site.name,
    description: "[same as above]",
    type: "article",
  },
};

export default function [Name]GuidePage() {
  return (
    <div className="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
      <nav className="mb-6 text-sm text-ink-500">
        <Link href="/" className="hover:text-brand-600">Home</Link>
        <span className="mx-2">/</span>
        <Link href="/guides" className="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</Link>
        <span className="mx-2">/</span>
        <span className="text-ink-700">[Short Title]</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold text-ink-900 sm:text-4xl">[Guide Title]</h1>
      <p className="mt-2 text-ink-500 text-sm">Last updated: [Month Year]</p>

      <article className="prose mt-8">
        {/* CONTENT HERE */}
      </article>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Step 2: Write Content (1500-2500 words)

### Structure Template

1. **Hook/Problem Statement** (100 words) — Start with the specific problem the reader has
2. **Quick Answer** (50 words) — Give the TL;DR upfront for featured snippet potential
3. **Infographic** — Generate and embed a visual summary
4. **Detailed Explanation** (400-600 words) — Deep dive into the concept
5. **Concrete Case Study** (300-400 words) — Real numbers, real scenario
6. **Comparison Table** — At least one data table comparing options
7. **Step-by-Step Guide** (200-300 words) — Actionable steps
8. **Calculator CTA** — Link to the relevant CalcWise calculator
9. **FAQ Section** (200-300 words) — 3-5 questions with JSON-LD schema

### Content Quality Rules

- Every section must contain specific dollar amounts, percentages, or timeframes
- Include at least ONE detailed case study with a persona:
  ```
  Example: "Marcus, a 32-year-old software engineer earning $95,000/year,
  wants to buy a home in Denver (median price: $550,000)..."
  ```
- Include at least ONE comparison table:
  ```tsx
  <div className="overflow-x-auto my-6">
    <table className="w-full text-sm border border-ink-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <thead className="bg-ink-100">
        <tr>
          <th className="px-4 py-2 text-left">Option</th>
          <th className="px-4 py-2 text-right">Monthly Cost</th>
          <th className="px-4 py-2 text-right">Total Over 5 Years</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>...</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  ```
- Link to relevant CalcWise calculators naturally:
  ```tsx
  <p>
    Use our <Link href="/calculators/mortgage" className="text-brand-600 underline">
    mortgage calculator</Link> to run your own numbers.
  </p>
  ```
- NO generic advice without numbers
- NO emoji anywhere
- NO filler paragraphs

### Infographic Generation

Generate at least 1 infographic per guide:

```bash
node ~/.cursor/skills/kie-image/generate.mjs "[descriptive prompt]" "3:2" --resolution 2K
```

Good infographic prompts for guides:
- Decision flowcharts ("Should I rent or buy?")
- Comparison visuals (side-by-side scenarios)
- Timeline/milestone graphics (savings journey)
- Breakdown charts (where does your money go)

Download and embed:
```bash
curl -o public/images/guides/[slug]-infographic.png "[URL]"
```

### FAQ with JSON-LD

At the end of the article, add FAQ section with schema:

```tsx
import { FaqJsonLd } from "@/components/FaqJsonLd";

const faqs = [
  { question: "...", answer: "..." },
  // 3-5 FAQs
];

// In the component:
<FaqJsonLd faqs={faqs} />
<section className="mt-12">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
    <div key={i} className="mt-6">
      <h3>{faq.question}</h3>
      <p>{faq.answer}</p>
    </div>
  ))}
</section>
```

## Step 3: Update Sitemap

Add to `src/app/sitemap.ts` if guides section doesn't auto-generate yet. Or add the guide to a guides data file if one exists.

## Step 4: Verify & Commit

```bash
npm run build
git add -A && git commit -m "Add guide: [title]"
```

## Target Keywords for Guides (priority order)

### Mortgage-related
- "how much house can I afford on [salary] salary"
- "is it better to pay off mortgage early or invest"
- "how much down payment do I need for a house"
- "15 year vs 30 year mortgage which is better"
- "how to get a lower mortgage rate"

### Savings-related
- "how to save [amount] in [timeframe]"
- "where to keep emergency fund for best interest"
- "high yield savings account vs CD which is better"
- "how much to save each month by age"
- "compound interest examples real life"

### Debt-related
- "how to pay off [amount] credit card debt fast"
- "debt avalanche vs snowball which is better"
- "should I consolidate my debt"
- "how long to pay off student loans"
- "balance transfer card vs personal loan for debt"

### Retirement-related
- "how much do I need to retire at [age]"
- "401k vs Roth IRA which is better"
- "am I saving enough for retirement"
- "FIRE movement how much do I need"
- "retirement savings by age benchmarks"

### General finance
- "50/30/20 budget rule explained with examples"
- "how to start investing with [amount]"
- "index fund vs individual stocks for beginners"
- "net worth by age average vs median"
